  "name": "Interferon Gamma Release Assay - TB Gold QuantiFERON",
  "code": "IGRA",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Result</span></div></th><th><div><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Interpretation</span></div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Positive</span></div></td><td><div><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Indicates a significant IFN-gamma response to the TB antigens, which may suggest active TB infection or latent TB infection.</span></div></td></tr><tr><td><div><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Negative</span></div></td><td><div><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Indicates no significant IFN-gamma response to the TB antigens, which may suggest the patient has not been exposed to TB or has not developed an immune response to it.</span></div></td></tr><tr><td><div><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Indeterminate</span></div></td><td><div><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Can occur due to technical error in the testing process or when the IFN-gamma response falls within a certain range that does not allow for a clear interpretation of the result. In these cases, the test may need to be repeated.</span></div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
